-- scripts/dst/run_report_dst.ail
--
-- WI-A14 piece 3 acceptance, under ADR-001 D11.
--
-- ============================================================================
-- What this suite claims, and what it deliberately does NOT
-- ============================================================================
--
-- It claims the REPORT and its GATE are correct: D11's field list is carried,
-- class-reached and branch-reached are separate counters read from D3's
-- catalogue, every rejection rule fires on its own single-field mutant, and a
-- complete report survives.
--
-- It does NOT claim a MEASURED coverage number for today's suite. Feeding these
-- counters from a real seed sweep is WI-A15's corpora work, and a script that
-- invented a number here would be reporting a measurement it never took —
-- which is the failure mode this project has spent twelve clusters learning to
-- avoid. What stands in for it is `documented_coverage()`: a DECLARED register,
-- sourced per class from the cluster reports and the catalogue, asserted
-- complete against `required_class_ids()` and asserted to keep the three
-- unreached classes in THREE DIFFERENT statuses.
--
-- ============================================================================
-- The three-reasons obligation, which is the thing tidying destroys
-- ============================================================================
--
-- Cluster 12: three classes are unreached for three different reasons, and a
-- single "unreached" number states three facts as one. `ReachStatus` gives each
-- its own constructor with a reason, and `scenario_three_gaps_three_reasons`
-- asserts they do not collapse — that the three carry three DISTINCT reach ids,
-- and that none of them is `waived`, because a waiver is a permission and a gap
-- is not.

module scripts/dst/run_report_dst

